},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The vertices are ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"text":", and the columns, the hyperedges, are at positions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<hyperedgeCount"},{"text":". The matrix conforms to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraph"},{"text":", so the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraphs"},{"text":" algorithms run","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on it unchanged. It is not a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"text":", even when built from one, because a cell edit can give a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"column any number of bits.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A column is any set of vertices. Empty columns and repeated columns are kept. A graph’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"self-loop becomes the one bit at its vertex, the hyperedge {v}. ","type":"text"},{"code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the directed form, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"UndirectedIncidenceList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the sparse representation of the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hypergraphs.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Storage","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Storage"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both orientations are stored: n rows of ⌈m\/64⌉ words and m columns of ⌈n\/64⌉ words, with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row and column popcounts cached. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"members(ofHyperedgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentHyperedges(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BitSet"},{"type":"text","text":" copy of ⌈n\/64⌉ or ⌈m\/64⌉ words, a cell edit writes two bits in O(1), and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transposed()"},{"type":"text","text":", the dual, swaps the two orientations in O(1). The storage is 2·n·m\/8 bytes, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the matrix suits dense or small incidence, such as spectral work or hypergraphs with large"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hyperedges. Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedIncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":" for sparse incidence."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Equality compares cell for cell, with equal shape, so column order counts.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedIncidenceList"},{"text":"’s equality ignores positions.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/incidencematrix"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/IncidenceMatrix/init(_:)-4zxvg":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The incidence matrix of a hypergraph: rows by vertex index, a column per hyperedge in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"hyperedges","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/init(_:)-4zxvg","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hypergraph","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols10HypergraphP"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/incidencematrix\/init(_:)-4zxvg","title":"init(_:)","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/do